## TokenLighten MCP (compact)

Three tools, nothing else: `read_file`, `edit_file`, `search_files`. Unknown file task (incl. unknown-location/multi-file discovery)=>`read_file mode=task_pack query="<verbatim request>"` before any Read/Grep/cat or Explore-style subagent; never truncate. Search: `action=find query=<one identifier>`; several=>ONE `queries=[…]`, never serial; set `path` to a known fixture/package subtree, repo-wide only if scope is unknown.
Workspace write safety: pass your own `cwd` on EVERY call — an undeclared root=>`cwd-required-for-edit`, never assume one; shared workspace=>each agent's own fixed `lane`.
An unrecognized `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report it, issue no edit, never infer from its fields.
A `read.receipt` is never a dead end or a re-pack cue: follow its `next`. Every `next`/hint a response advertises is executable — run it verbatim; never invent or template-fill your own continuation.
Everything else — artifact/archive specifics, verification-kit detail, per-kind deep rules — arrives on-demand inside the response that needs it; this is the complete ruleset only until one does.
